        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "Both MCUs are unpowered, so the board will not function.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE2", "HSE3", "FCC2", "NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["HSE2.1", "HSE2.3", "FCC2.5", "FCC2.37", "HSE3.1", "HSE3.3", "NAVC2.5", "NAVC2.6"],
      "nets": ["NET0104", "Net-(C20-Pad1)", "NET0062", "NET0125", "Net-(C109-Pad1)", "Net-(NAVC2-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC2-PH1)"],
      "observed": "HSE2 is connected between FCC2 pins PE6 (pin 5) and PE7 (pin 37), not the HSE pins PH0/PH1. HSE3 is connected only to C102, C109, and R94, and is not connected to NAVC2 PH0/PH1.",
      "expected": "Each 25 MHz HSE crystal should connect between the MCU's PH0/PH1 oscillator pins (FCC2 pins 12/13, NAVC2 pins 5/6).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) on net NET0104 with (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"HSE3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) on net NET0125 with only C102"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) on net Net-(NAVC2-PH0) with only C103"}
      ],
      "impact": "MCUs will not have a stable external clock, preventing proper operation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U9"],
      "pins": ["U9.7"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V"],
      "observed": "BMI088 PS pin (pin 7) is tied to +3.3V.",
      "expected": "For I2C operation (spec: 'I2C addr 0x19 (acc) / 0x69 (gyr)'), PS must be tied to GND to select I2C mode.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PS\") (pintype \"input\")) on net +3.3V"}
      ],
      "impact": "IMU will be in SPI mode, so I2C communication with the IMU will fail.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies. The most critical is that the 3.3V rail is split into two unconnected nets (+3.3V and +3V3) and the MCU VDD pins are left unconnected, so the MCUs are unpowered. Additionally, the HSE crystals are miswired, and the BMI088 PS pin is tied high, selecting SPI instead of I2C."
}

